<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia84437c12d52535d5f7dd634fa7e9be38b55b729" commit="72eba918a059c7fadbf3c574e5dfc4326111050a" commit_message="input_playback: Add emulated stylus support  This patch introduces a new emulated stylus device which matches the internal display resolution and is mainly for click emulation.  BUG=chromium:702532 TEST=none  Change-Id: Ia84437c12d52535d5f7dd634fa7e9be38b55b729 Signed-off-by: Chung-yih Wang &lt;cywang@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/469509 Reviewed-by: Chi-Ngai Wan &lt;cnwan@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Cheng &lt;bccheng@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="469509" owner_email="cywang@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/09/469509/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6caaac96e761810177733f8e929eaae553d6931c" commit="ccbbaddd2b9080ddac43e0d9270b5692efd18ae2" commit_message="autotest: Update BUG_TEMPLATE for desktopui_MashLogin  CC the mustash autotest bugs mailing list for new bugs  BUG=none TEST=manually tested CC-ing the mailing list from crbug.com  Change-Id: I6caaac96e761810177733f8e929eaae553d6931c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/469131 Commit-Ready: James Cook &lt;jamescook@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: James Cook &lt;jamescook@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Xiyuan Xia &lt;xiyuan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="469131" owner_email="jamescook@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/31/469131/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I727c7231ead7682a35036eb9eb4e9e714a6f979f" commit="f084eed0c0dbd5d52942f82cd11ef0012db48710" commit_message="crash: Tag chrome --mash crashes as product Chrome_ChromeOS  This allows the crash dashboard to use chrome-specific tooling and ensures the crashes show up in chrome crash triage.  Also tag the process type as &quot;mash&quot; to differentiate it from browser and renderer crashes.  BUG=chromium:704180 TEST=unit test added, manually trigger crash of chrome mash process, manually force upload, crash dashboard shows product Chrome_ChromeOS  Change-Id: I727c7231ead7682a35036eb9eb4e9e714a6f979f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/459117 Commit-Ready: James Cook &lt;jamescook@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: James Cook &lt;jamescook@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="459117" owner_email="jamescook@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/17/459117/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4bf9967cc3ce4961b5ef90c2cbae5a769ece7fd2" commit="c38ec27263b240a976558f971623e83289ec6ae7" commit_message="Add dependencies to chromeos-firmware-1.ebuild.  In order to build FW from source (on FW branch), just add bootimage USE flag to the overlay's configuration (and cros_ec USE flag when applicable). On ToT keep overriding virtual/chromeos-firmware/chromeos-firmware-3.ebuild to pull in pre- built FW from BCS.  Add dependencies to chromeos-bootimage and chromeos-ec when bootimage/cros_ec USE variables are defined instead of always pointing to chromeos-firmware-null. This makes managing FW for overlays quite a bit simpler.  BUG=b:36870038, TEST=If it exists, remove virtual/chromeos-firmware folder, then      USE=&quot;-bootimage -cros_ec&quot; emerge-${BOARD} -ep --tree chromeos-firmware        Verify that chromeos-firmware-null is used.      USE=&quot;bootimage cros_ec&quot; emerge-${BOARD} -ep --tree chromeos-firmware        Verify that chromeos-bootimage and chromeos-ec are used.  Change-Id: I4bf9967cc3ce4961b5ef90c2cbae5a769ece7fd2 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/467826 Commit-Ready: YH Lin &lt;yueherngl@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Patrick Berny &lt;pberny@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: YH Lin &lt;yueherngl@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="467826" owner_email="pberny@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/26/467826/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib67e2cd75d5405a0d8a84634ce5f3727a34dd094" commit="5320b48c12a269910df6302ef29136e5c25a851c" commit_message="Fix net_utils.FindUnusedTCPPort.  The code did not properly closed the TCPServer, and was relying on GC to release the port before the returned port is actually used.  Actually starting a TCPServer is also unnecessary since we only need to bind the port but not listen, and TCPServer would do both.  Listening only on LOCALHOST also cause problem sometimes, since some code use the returned port to bind on 0.0.0.0.  Change this to open a socket, bind it on 0.0.0.0 port 0, and return the bound port after closing it. There always would be race condition if the port is used by others between the port is returned and actually used by caller, but since almost all usage of this function is in unittest, and the chance of race condition is very small, this can be ignored.  BUG=chromium:665306 TEST=make test  Change-Id: Ib67e2cd75d5405a0d8a84634ce5f3727a34dd094 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/469531 Commit-Ready: Pi-Hsun Shih &lt;pihsun@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Pi-Hsun Shih &lt;pihsun@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Pi-Hsun Shih &lt;pihsun@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="469531" owner_email="pihsun@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/31/469531/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="9436.0.0-rc2"/></manifest>